Answer: An additional nextLine() must be called after nextInt() to remove the remaining newline character.

```java
int number = scan.nextInt();
scan.nextLine();
String name = scan.nextLine();
```

The first nextLine() removes the newline character. The second nextLine() takes the required string input.

Answer: First, a string is taken using next(). Then charAt(0) is used to take the first character.

```java
String input = scan.next();
char character = input.charAt(0);
```

next() belongs to the Scanner class, while charAt() belongs to the String class.

